{{also|verlies}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gml|de}} {{m|gml|verlies||loss}}, cognate with {{cog|nl|verlies||id.}} and pertaining to German {{m|de|verlieren||to lose}}. Apparently, the original meaning is “place where someone is lost”; possibly a second word (like “place”, “hole”) has been omitted, although no such compound seems to be attested.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/fɛɐ̯ˈliːs/|/fɐˈliːs/|lang=de}}
* {{homophones|lang=de|verließ}}
* {{rhymes|iːs|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|n|Verlieses|Verliese|Verlieschen}}

# [[dungeon]] {{gloss|historic prison in a vault}}
#: ''Gefangene Feinde ließ man in '''Verliesen''' unterhalb der Burg verhungern.''
#:: Captured enemies were starved to death in '''dungeons''' below the castle.
# an [[underground]] [[prison]] or place of [[captivity]]
#: ''Der Entführer hielt sein Opfer in einem eigens gebauten '''Verlies''' im Keller seines Hauses.''
#:: The kidnapper held his victim in a specially built '''prison''' in the basement of his house.

